<h1>Guideline Pricing: Complete 2026 Breakdown</h1>

<p>Guideline is an enterprise media planning intelligence platform aggregating approximately $200 billion in annual global media spend across 65 countries. It provides AI-powered planning tools, transactional rate data from agency billing systems, and is used by over 90% of top global media companies. Guideline does not publish pricing — it operates on a custom enterprise contract model.</p>

<h2>Pricing Model</h2>

<p>Guideline uses a <strong>custom enterprise subscription model</strong>. Pricing is not disclosed publicly and is negotiated based on:</p>

<ul>
<li>Organization size and media spend under management</li>
<li>Geographic scope (number of markets accessed)</li>
<li>Number of users and seats</li>
<li>Modules licensed (AI Factory, AI Agent, Local Dynamics, MCP Server, etc.)</li>
<li>Integration requirements with existing agency systems</li>
</ul>

<p>Given Guideline's positioning serving the largest global media agencies and holding companies, entry-level enterprise pricing is likely in the six-figure annual range. No third-party pricing benchmarks are publicly available.</p>

